---
layout: layouts/app.njk
title: "Backup"
description: "Download a JSON snapshot of every profile in this browser. The fastest path to disaster recovery if the device dies."
permalink: /app/backup/
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{% from "partials/app-toolbar.njk" import appToolbar %}
{% from "partials/page-info.njk" import pageInfo %}
{# U1. The page was five stacked cards, three of them pure prose. A
   paragraph in a full-width card stops at the global 70ch measure, so
   two thirds of the page was text and the right third of every prose
   card was empty. The prose is in the info modal now and the page is
   one surface: the two things you can actually download, and how long
   it has been since you last did. #}
<div class="app-page app-page--dense app-page--fill" x-data="backupView()" x-init="refresh()">
  {% call appToolbar("Backup") %}
    <div class="app-toolbar__group">
      <span class="app-toolbar__context">Last backup: <span x-text="lastBackupLabel()"></span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="app-toolbar__actions">
      {% call pageInfo(id="backup", title="About backups", label="What a backup contains and where it goes") %}
        <p>Everything you've entered lives in this browser's localStorage. If the device dies, the cache gets wiped, or you switch browsers, the only way back is a JSON file you downloaded earlier. Take one every week.</p>
        <h3>What gets backed up</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Every profile in this browser (not just the active one)</li>
          <li>All accounts, categories, transactions, payees, goals, recurring templates, snapshots</li>
          <li>Per-profile settings: theme picks, group collapse state, table sort preferences</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The file is plain JSON. Open it in any text editor, store it in Dropbox / iCloud / Google Drive, attach it to an email to yourself - all of these are valid backup strategies.</p>
        <h3>Restore</h3>
        <p>If you need to bring a backup back into the app, use <a href="/app/import/">/app/import/</a>. Drop the file in, pick "Import as new" (keeps your current data) or "Replace this profile", and you're back where you were.</p>
        <h3>Backup hygiene</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Weekly cadence</strong> - set a calendar reminder.</li>
          <li><strong>Multiple destinations</strong> - local disk + a cloud folder is the minimum.</li>
          <li><strong>Test restores quarterly</strong> - open one of your backups in a fresh browser to confirm it actually loads.</li>
          <li><strong>Encrypt at rest</strong> if the backup folder isn't already encrypted (Cryptomator / OS-native FDE / VeraCrypt all work).</li>
        </ul>
      {% endcall %}
    </div>
  {% endcall %}

  <div class="panel backup-panel app-grow" :class="reminderClass()">
    <div class="panel__head">
      <h2 class="panel__title">Take a backup</h2>
      <div class="panel__actions">
        <span class="backup-panel__msg" x-show="lastDownloadMsg" x-cloak x-text="lastDownloadMsg"></span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="panel__body backup-panel__body">
      <p class="backup-panel__rec" x-text="recommendation()"></p>

      <div class="backup-actions">
        <div class="backup-action">
          <h3 class="backup-action__title">Every profile in this browser</h3>
          <p class="backup-action__body">Recommended. One bundle with all profiles, all transactions, and all settings. Restore one or all from <a href="/app/import/">/app/import/</a>.</p>
          <button class="btn btn--primary" type="button"
                  @click="backupAll()" :disabled="!hasProfiles"
                  data-tip="Bundles every profile in this browser into a single JSON file."
                  x-text="hasProfiles ? ('Download bundle (' + profileCount + ' profile' + (profileCount === 1 ? '' : 's') + ')') : 'No profiles to back up'"></button>
        </div>
        <div class="backup-action">
          <h3 class="backup-action__title">Active profile only</h3>
          <p class="backup-action__body">A smaller file containing just the currently-open profile. Useful when you want to share or move one budget without exposing the others.</p>
          <button class="btn btn--secondary" type="button"
                  @click="backupActive()" :disabled="!hasActiveProfile"
                  data-tip="Downloads only the profile currently open in the sidebar.">
            <span x-text="hasActiveProfile ? ('Download ' + activeName) : 'No active profile'"></span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="backup-panel__note">Both options download a plain JSON file. Save it somewhere you trust: a cloud folder, an external drive, or both.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
function backupView() {
  return {
    lastBackup: null,
    lastDownloadMsg: "",
    /* refresh() previously snapshotted the store into local fields,
       but the snapshot ran ONCE at Alpine init — before the async
       Dexie profile restore completed. Result: "No profiles to back
       up" persisted even after the active profile loaded. Convert
       to getters that read the store live; Alpine tracks the deps
       inside the binding expression and re-evaluates on store
       mutations via _listVersion. */
    get hasProfiles() {
      var s = this.$store.budget;
      if (!s) return false;
      void s._listVersion;
      return !!(s.profiles && s.profiles.length);
    },
    get hasActiveProfile() {
      var s = this.$store.budget;
      if (!s) return false;
      void s._listVersion;
      return !!s.profile;
    },
    get profileCount() {
      var s = this.$store.budget;
      if (!s) return 0;
      void s._listVersion;
      return s.profiles ? s.profiles.length : 0;
    },
    get activeName() {
      var s = this.$store.budget;
      if (!s) return "";
      void s._listVersion;
      return s.profile ? s.profile.name : "";
    },
    refresh() {
      /* Only the lastBackup field still needs imperative refresh —
         it lives in localStorage, not the store, so it's not part of
         Alpine's reactive graph. */
      try { this.lastBackup = localStorage.getItem("projectbudget:lastBackupAt"); }
      catch (_e) { this.lastBackup = null; }
    },
    daysSince() {
      if (!this.lastBackup) return Infinity;
      var ms = Date.now() - new Date(this.lastBackup).getTime();
      return ms / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24);
    },
    lastBackupLabel() {
      if (!this.lastBackup) return "Never";
      var d = new Date(this.lastBackup);
      var days = this.daysSince();
      if (days < 1)  return "Today — " + d.toLocaleTimeString();
      if (days < 2)  return "Yesterday — " + d.toLocaleTimeString();
      return Math.floor(days) + " days ago — " + d.toLocaleDateString();
    },
    recommendation() {
      var d = this.daysSince();
      if (!isFinite(d)) return "Take your first backup now. A single download covers you for the next week.";
      if (d < 7)  return "You're in good shape. Next reminder in " + Math.ceil(7 - d) + " day" + (Math.ceil(7 - d) === 1 ? "" : "s") + ".";
      if (d < 30) return "It's been over a week — refresh your backup.";
      return "It's been over a month. Take a fresh backup before you make more changes.";
    },
    /* Rail colour on the one panel. Renamed off card-- when the page
       stopped being a stack of cards. */
    reminderClass() {
      var d = this.daysSince();
      if (!isFinite(d) || d >= 30) return "backup-panel--danger";
      if (d >= 7) return "backup-panel--warn";
      return "backup-panel--ok";
    },
    backupAll() {
      this.$store.budget.exportAllProfilesJSON();
      this._markDownloaded("Bundle downloaded.");
    },
    backupActive() {
      if (!this.$store.budget.profile) return;
      this.$store.budget.exportActiveJSON();
      this._markDownloaded("Active profile downloaded.");
    },
    _markDownloaded(msg) {
      try { localStorage.setItem("projectbudget:lastBackupAt", new Date().toISOString()); }
      catch (_e) {}
      this.lastDownloadMsg = msg;
      var self = this;
      setTimeout(function () { self.lastDownloadMsg = ""; }, 3500);
      this.refresh();
    },
  };
}
</script>

<style>
  /* One surface, with a rail whose colour says how overdue you are. */
  .backup-panel { display: flex; flex-direction: column; border-left: 4px solid var(--border); }
  .backup-panel--ok     { border-left-color: var(--ok); }
  .backup-panel--warn   { border-left-color: var(--warn); }
  .backup-panel--danger { border-left-color: var(--danger); }
  .backup-panel__body { flex: 1 1 auto; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-md); }
  /* The global p { max-width: 70ch } is what left the old prose cards
     two thirds full. These two lines belong to the panel, so they get
     the panel's width. */
  .backup-panel__rec { margin: 0; max-width: none; font-size: var(--fs-lg); }
  .backup-panel__note { margin: 0; max-width: none; color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: var(--fs-sm); }
  .backup-panel__msg { color: var(--ok); font-size: var(--fs-sm); }
  .backup-actions { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-md); }
  @media (max-width: 899px) { .backup-actions { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  /* Block surfaces take the page's own ground now (2026-09-04):
     a tinted box on a plain canvas is the seam the app chrome removes.
     The hairline border is what separates it. */
  .backup-action { display: flex; flex-direction: column; padding: var(--space-md); background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-soft); border-radius: var(--radius-input); }
  .backup-action .btn { margin-top: auto; align-self: flex-start; }
  .backup-action__title { margin: 0 0 var(--space-2xs); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--fs-lg); }
  .backup-action__body { margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm); max-width: none; color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: var(--fs-sm); line-height: 1.5; }
</style>
